1
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:07,810
(Morning of Day 7)

2
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:27,060
(Mokgye is alone and lost in thought.)

3
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:30,030
I'll tell you what I find weird.

4
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:32,100
That was on the agenda.

5
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,240
Applying the points
from the Majority Rules Game...

6
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,040
to the vote.

7
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:37,440
Team Red was against it.

8
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,910
But I don't get it.

9
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:42,310
They won the MVP twice, and they...

10
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:43,780
But they were against it.

11
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:45,680
Team White thought about it
and also objected to it.

12
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:47,820
Another thing I witnessed...

13
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:49,550
was that Team Red would give...

14
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:52,250
- Team Blue seven credits.
- Why?

15
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:54,360
- Why?
- Why would Team Red...

16
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:55,360
I don't get that part.

17
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,720
And Team White suddenly went,

18
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,590
"We'll give you,"
and gave her ten credits.

19
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:02,830
That means White and Blue are
still an alliance.

20
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:04,830
But why would Team Red give them
to Team Blue?

21
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:07,570
- I don't understand that either.
- Exactly.

22
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:10,470
- I don't get it.
- That means there's a deal,

23
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:11,670
and I find that odd.

24
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:16,980
Did you sleep well?

25
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,620
Yesterday, I feel like...

26
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:23,180
we were too exclusive.

27
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:25,650
- When Maillard...
- Yes.

28
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:28,620
- offered to join us,
- Should we have accepted?

29
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:29,760
we should have accepted.

30
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,160
Why didn't we?

31
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:34,530
Based on the information we had yesterday,
it was a tough decision.

32
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:37,900
- Yes, we thought we were at an advantage.
- We thought so.

33
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,540
When you think about it, we were cheeky,

34
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:43,940
thinking that we had the upper hand,
and they were all bad choices.

35
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:45,570
I feel like we were...

36
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:48,340
a bit arrogant yesterday.

37
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:50,850
How about this, then?

38
00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:52,980
When the casting voter has the power,

39
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,950
we can give Team Red more gold.

40
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:57,550
- That's a gain for them.
- If we do that,

41
00:01:57,550 --> 00:02:01,620
it's likely going to be an ultimatum.

42
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:03,930
And we overlooked that fact.

43
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,160
The Ultimatum Game is...

44
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:09,760
is a classic game theory experiment
in economics.

45
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:13,270
The game involves two players...

46
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:16,740
sharing 1,000 dollars,

47
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:18,770
with one acting as the proposer...

48
00:02:18,770 --> 00:02:22,140
and the other as the responder.

49
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:24,510
The proposer is allowed...

50
00:02:24,510 --> 00:02:27,720
to freely offer a single division ratio...

51
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:31,620
of the 1,000 dollars to the responder,

52
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:34,960
who can only choose...

53
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,660
to either accept or reject the proposal.

54
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:40,190
If the responder accepts,

55
00:02:40,190 --> 00:02:42,830
both players divide the 1,000 dollars...

56
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:44,900
according to the proposed ratio.

57
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:47,170
If the responder rejects the offer,

58
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:51,210
neither player receives a single penny.

59
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:55,640
Generally, one might expect
a 5-to-5 split.

60
00:02:55,940 --> 00:02:58,880
However, even if the proposer offers
a 9-to-1 ratio,

61
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:03,550
rejecting it results in a payout
of zero for both sides.

62
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:05,490
Therefore,
accepting any offered proportion...

63
00:03:05,490 --> 00:03:10,020
yields a greater benefit
to the responder than rejecting it.

64
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:13,730
Nevertheless, if the proposer presents...

65
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:16,930
an overwhelmingly unfair ratio
like 9 to 1,

66
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:19,730
the responder may choose
to reject the offer,

67
00:03:19,730 --> 00:03:23,140
adopting the mindset...

68
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:25,870
of "I'd rather get nothing
than let you have anything."

69
00:03:26,570 --> 00:03:28,540
To mitigate this risk,

70
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:31,680
the proposer may strategically choose...

71
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:35,850
to offer a higher share
to the responder from the start.

72
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:40,220
If Team Red becomes too powerful
as the casting voter,

73
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,790
they can say, "It's better to win..."

74
00:03:43,790 --> 00:03:46,630
"at least 10 or 100 dollars..."

75
00:03:46,630 --> 00:03:49,800
"rather than to be left with nothing.
Give us a bigger proportion."

76
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,630
- Right.
- Last night, I asked Ugong...

77
00:03:51,630 --> 00:03:54,740
if he'd be left with nothing...

78
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:57,710
or give them 900 dollars
only to get 100 dollars instead.

79
00:03:57,710 --> 00:04:01,140
And he was very flustered.

80
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,440
I'd get 100 dollars.

81
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,010
I could buy grilled chicken feet,
at least.

82
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:08,520
The closed-off approach we took...

83
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:11,620
to protect our prize money...

84
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:13,990
could have put us...

85
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:18,030
at an absurd disadvantage
in the Ultimatum Game.

86
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:23,930
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

87
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:27,570
Team leaders can now be changed.

88
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:31,570
Discuss whether to reappoint
the current leader.

89
00:04:32,570 --> 00:04:34,810
We're reappointing the leaders now.

90
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,650
The people who went yesterday were...

91
00:04:37,650 --> 00:04:40,450
me, you, and Luna.

92
00:04:40,450 --> 00:04:44,720
The three of us hastily rejected it.

93
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:48,320
We'll say,
"We told our teammates about that."

94
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,160
And we were outraged like,
"Why did you do that?"

95
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,760
- "I love Maillard."
- "Ugong and Maetel..."

96
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,030
"got very angry."

97
00:04:53,030 --> 00:04:56,100
"Why didn't you accept that?"

98
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,800
We'll say sorry
and try to bring them around.

99
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,100
I don't think that's a good idea.

100
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,240
- No?
- It won't work.

101
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,440
I can picture the situation,

102
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:04,710
but think about it.

103
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:08,440
Team Red's leader is motivated
by his benefits.

104
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:11,280
We'd look too desperate
if we went so far as to change...

105
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:13,010
the leader to ask him again.

106
00:05:13,010 --> 00:05:14,280
- He won't join us, then.
- We'll look too desperate.

107
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:16,150
That would make us look so lame.

108
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:18,220
I think he'll be angrier...

109
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:20,550
- because he can see through us.
- It was like a clean fishbowl.

110
00:05:20,550 --> 00:05:22,560
- It's way too obvious.
- We might be...

111
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:25,490
better off apologizing sincerely.

112
00:05:25,490 --> 00:05:28,700
If he's still willing to trade with us,

113
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:31,570
- we can offer him a good deal.
- Right.

114
00:05:31,570 --> 00:05:33,230
I agree with you, but...

115
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,840
- yesterday...
- Look. This is a book I'm reading.

116
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:37,640
- I'll read you the chapter title.
- It was just such a good offer.

117
00:05:37,910 --> 00:05:40,170
"If you reveal it all at once,
there is no tomorrow."

118
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:42,740
- That's what it says.
- I'm serious.

119
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:44,880
- What's that?
- It contains helpful stuff.

120
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:47,250
- "The Art of Worldly Wisdom."
- What's that book?

121
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:49,150
Just read the chapter titles.
It's helpful.

122
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,550
"Hide your hand,"

123
00:05:50,550 --> 00:05:52,050
- That's right.
- and overwhelm with silence."

124
00:05:52,050 --> 00:05:54,190
We need to be quiet.
We've been too talkative.

125
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,900
Maillard shaved.

126
00:06:04,170 --> 00:06:05,370
- It's Maillard 2.0.
- Did he?

127
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:06,600
You're 2.0 now.

128
00:06:07,070 --> 00:06:08,340
It was about time I shaved.

129
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,300
You just shaved it off.

130
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:14,140
Today, we have...

131
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,080
a major event.

132
00:06:20,310 --> 00:06:23,750
- Hi. About what you said yesterday,
- Yes.

133
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:25,290
- we decided to go with it.
- Okay.

134
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:27,190
We want to keep it at one-eighth...

135
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:30,320
and stick to your proposal.

136
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:33,390
(Maillard rendezvoused with the leaders
of Team Blue and Team White.)

137
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:36,000
(We're going to use Team White's skill,
Digital Currency Issuance Authority.)

138
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:38,400
We're going to issue digital currency.

139
00:06:40,030 --> 00:06:42,870
We're going to increase
the money supply...

140
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:44,410
to an unimaginable point.

141
00:06:44,910 --> 00:06:48,180
They have 198 diamonds, right?

142
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:50,340
- We're going to turn them...
- Into trash?

143
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:53,050
into pennies
so that they can only afford food.

144
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:55,380
We can't buy the skill
unless Team Black cooperates, though.

145
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:56,380
I have...

146
00:06:57,650 --> 00:07:01,220
(I've brought him into my inner circle.)

147
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,260
Yes.

148
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:05,790
Without him, it won't be so easy to win.

149
00:07:05,790 --> 00:07:06,890
You're right about that.

150
00:07:06,890 --> 00:07:08,460
We've come to accept that.

151
00:07:08,460 --> 00:07:10,770
How are you going to pay Donkey?

152
00:07:10,770 --> 00:07:12,130
I'll tell you about that now.

153
00:07:12,130 --> 00:07:14,170
Right now, Black...

154
00:07:14,170 --> 00:07:15,200
has no prize money.

155
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:19,170
So, he has to sell more weapons.

156
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:21,640
You're presuming a war.

157
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:24,250
Yes. The war has to be part of it.

158
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:27,420
- Yes, I understand.
- And these two...

159
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:30,380
One of the conditions of the offer was...

160
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:32,320
to bring Black...

161
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:35,220
back into our group.

162
00:07:35,790 --> 00:07:38,160
It looks like he wants Donkey...

163
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:41,230
to win some prize money within the system.

164
00:07:42,030 --> 00:07:44,900
But to do that, the only method is...

165
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:46,000
going to war.

166
00:07:47,970 --> 00:07:49,540
I'm torn.

167
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,940
If you decide to join us,

168
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:55,440
we're going to distribute the diamonds...

169
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:57,210
evenly and fairly.

170
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:01,950
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)

171
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:03,980
I think it'll be okay,

172
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:07,120
but we did talk about that.

173
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:10,190
"Is it fair to give Donkey
an even amount?"

174
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:12,790
Some had that idea.

175
00:08:12,790 --> 00:08:15,200
- Okay.
- Because we can't know...

176
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,230
what role he played...

177
00:08:17,230 --> 00:08:19,170
- Right.
- and how strong your bond is.

178
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:21,940
From an overall perspective,
he worked as a spy...

179
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:24,370
and handed Black the codes.

180
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:26,510
But if we say no to this condition,

181
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:29,010
- we can't maintain our alliance.
- That's true.

182
00:08:29,010 --> 00:08:31,810
But we maintain the status quo,
even if we don't go to war, right?

183
00:08:31,810 --> 00:08:33,880
And that's more advantageous.

184
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:36,420
- But we can't maintain the status quo...
- Yes?

185
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:38,820
because we gave them some diamonds...

186
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:40,390
- to ease their crunch.
- Okay.

187
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:44,190
Without the digital issuance,
we can't maintain the status quo.

188
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:46,630
- Without the new skill...
- Yes.

189
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:48,860
You have a daily issuance limit right now.

190
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:50,700
So, without Black...

191
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:52,230
Does he also want one-eighth?

192
00:08:52,670 --> 00:08:53,870
How ungrateful.

193
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:56,140
I didn't tell him
that we'd give him one-eighth yet.

194
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:58,510
But he was willing
to help the diamonds win.

195
00:08:58,510 --> 00:09:00,410
In that situation,

196
00:09:00,410 --> 00:09:03,680
we don't know what trick he'll pull
if he gets...

197
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,480
less than others.

198
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:07,980
I think we should stick
to the even shares.

199
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:09,380
If he were to pull a trick,

200
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:10,420
he'd have done it
regardless of the amount.

201
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:11,590
- Right.
- To be honest.

202
00:09:12,050 --> 00:09:14,990
That's why I want him
to get as little as possible.

203
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:17,960
- If he pulls something,
- Yes.

204
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,130
- I'll...
- You'll eliminate him?

205
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:20,430
He can just be the bad guy...

206
00:09:20,430 --> 00:09:23,360
because it's all tiring for me.
That's my opinion.

207
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:26,030
Your priority is
protecting Team Red, right?

208
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:28,440
No, it's protecting the community
right now.

209
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,770
I need all my teammates to survive.

210
00:09:30,770 --> 00:09:33,740
I want everyone but Team Gold...

211
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,340
to survive...

212
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,650
so that we'll be here on the last day
with the prize.

213
00:09:38,650 --> 00:09:40,180
That's my current goal.

214
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:42,820
I might be the only one...

215
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:44,990
who wants to get rid of the war.

216
00:09:44,990 --> 00:09:48,660
Some might want to use it as leverage.

217
00:09:49,190 --> 00:09:52,260
But I hate going to war,

218
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:54,260
and I still believe
we have to get rid of it...

219
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,800
in the long run.

220
00:09:57,630 --> 00:10:00,970
However, we can't fulfill that goal
unless we're the majority.

221
00:10:00,970 --> 00:10:02,340
We had no choice
but to join forces with them.

222
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:06,170
I think at that point,
ensuring my team's survival...

223
00:10:06,270 --> 00:10:08,880
had become my core principle.

224
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:12,110
Committed to that principle,

225
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:15,320
I thought that even if it meant
teaming up with Team Black,

226
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,020
I had to take a stand.

227
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:22,220
Is Ugong out again?

228
00:10:22,490 --> 00:10:24,060
- I don't know. He's not here.
- Where is he?

229
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:25,990
This is why I have my doubts about him.

230
00:10:25,990 --> 00:10:28,560
He does act in a way
that raises suspicion, to be honest.

231
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:30,330
But if he were a spy,

232
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:32,270
he wouldn't go out so much
after we warned him it looked suspicious.

233
00:10:32,270 --> 00:10:35,170
Seeing how he does it anyway,
I think he just likes being out.

234
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:39,770
I just walk.
I organize my thoughts while walking.

235
00:10:39,770 --> 00:10:41,540
Unlike yesterday,

236
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,880
I decided to take a different approach
to navigate the situation.

237
00:10:45,410 --> 00:10:47,780
I decided to pin my hopes on Team Red.

238
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:51,950
Who is it?

239
00:10:51,950 --> 00:10:53,650
- Hello.
- I'll be waiting at the Hub.

240
00:10:53,650 --> 00:10:54,860
- All right.
- Thanks.

241
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:58,890
I don't know why
Ugong keeps wandering around,

242
00:10:58,890 --> 00:11:01,760
but he was looking for Maillard.
He wants to talk to him.

243
00:11:05,970 --> 00:11:08,770
Did you sleep well?
I have something to tell you.

244
00:11:08,770 --> 00:11:10,300
- Sure.
- The thing is...

245
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:13,240
- I mean, situations keep changing anyway.
- Right.

246
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:16,940
So, I'd like to join Team Red for the day.

247
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:18,950
- I wonder if you would take me in...
- Yes?

248
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:20,280
if I apply for relocation.

249
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:22,680
- To Team Red?
- Yes.

250
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:26,390
It was my personal goal...

251
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:29,160
to find a way to survive
as winning with Team Gold seemed unlikely.

252
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:30,920
It also seemed reasonable
on a macro level...

253
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,260
because my joining Team Red...

254
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:36,130
would help strengthen solidarity...

255
00:11:36,130 --> 00:11:38,570
between Team Red and Team Gold.

256
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:42,000
I know you need to discuss it
with your team members.

257
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:46,270
But I'm planning
to apply for citizenship in Team Red.

258
00:11:46,270 --> 00:11:49,280
- I'll talk to them and let you know.
- Okay.

259
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:50,540
Please put in a good word for me.

260
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:53,880
It's not like I have some profound motive
behind this decision.

261
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:55,880
I'm just feeling a bit frustrated...

262
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:58,250
- just as I told you yesterday.
- Right.

263
00:11:58,250 --> 00:12:00,990
- And I believe you feel the same way.
- I understand.

264
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:02,820
- I'll apply for relocation.
- Okay.

265
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,240
Every single day,
something shocking happens here.

266
00:12:19,810 --> 00:12:21,210
I'd like to apply for relocation.

267
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:24,710
I'd like to move to Team Red.

268
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:26,550
Please.

269
00:12:29,450 --> 00:12:31,320
Ugong of Team Gold...

270
00:12:31,550 --> 00:12:33,990
has requested relocation to Team Red.

271
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:35,660
Will you accept his request?

272
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:36,820
Please give us a moment.

273
00:12:51,470 --> 00:12:53,010
It's taking them quite some time.

274
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,850
Please take me in.

275
00:13:04,690 --> 00:13:07,050
Please, I beg you.
It's taking you so long.

276
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,420
Gosh, seriously.

277
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:11,860
Oh, you're here.

278
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:13,890
I didn't want you to find out
through the system...

279
00:13:13,890 --> 00:13:15,200
- since you came to us this morning.
- I see.

280
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:18,500
My team members and I
talked things through.

281
00:13:18,530 --> 00:13:21,030
Some of them felt uneasy about it.

282
00:13:21,030 --> 00:13:22,200
- "Uneasy?"
- Yes.

283
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:24,300
They don't think this is the right time...

284
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:28,240
Then what could I do to earn your trust?

285
00:13:28,710 --> 00:13:30,980
- I'll be completely honest with you.
- Yes.

286
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,880
If you had requested it yesterday,

287
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:35,820
it would've been much easier
for us to decide.

288
00:13:36,950 --> 00:13:39,690
The discussion time
for leader reappointment has ended.

289
00:13:39,950 --> 00:13:42,020
If you have decided to change leaders,

290
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,890
the current and new leaders...

291
00:13:45,130 --> 00:13:47,860
must visit the Community Center together.

292
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,100
Oh, gosh.

293
00:13:49,730 --> 00:13:51,500
- What should we do? Ugong is...
- We should just...

294
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:54,200
- change our leader smoothly...
- Shouldn't we go out to look for him?

295
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:56,300
- If three of us agree,
- Yes.

296
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:58,570
that's a majority.

297
00:13:58,570 --> 00:13:59,840
Gosh, seriously.

298
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,640
Ugong's belongings are still here, right?

299
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:02,780
- His stuff is here.
- Yes, his stuff is here.

300
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:06,980
Honestly, I wanted a change of leader.

301
00:14:07,310 --> 00:14:11,490
I kept thinking
we needed a change within our team.

302
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:13,650
But since Ugong wasn't there,

303
00:14:14,190 --> 00:14:17,520
I didn't get to share my thoughts on that.

304
00:14:17,660 --> 00:14:18,990
I was just wondering to myself,

305
00:14:19,230 --> 00:14:22,030
"Will things just play out
the same as always?"

306
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:24,230
Then can't I take the lead today?

307
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,500
Then you take the lead today...

308
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:27,330
- and pass the baton to us tomorrow.
- Tomorrow...

309
00:14:27,330 --> 00:14:28,870
So, we'll take turns being the leader.

310
00:14:28,870 --> 00:14:30,000
Won't we change the leader today?

311
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,170
- I think I should keep the leadership.
- She's keeping the leadership today.

312
00:14:32,170 --> 00:14:34,170
- One of us will be the leader tomorrow.
- That's right.

313
00:14:34,170 --> 00:14:35,180
Okay.

314
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:38,580
Actually,
this is when all the teams gather.

315
00:14:38,910 --> 00:14:39,950
- Shall we go too?
- Shall we?

316
00:14:39,950 --> 00:14:41,380
- Shall we? Let's go.
- Some important information...

317
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:43,050
- might be floating around.
- You're right.

318
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:45,090
- When we go down there...
- Ugong seems to have quite the stamina.

319
00:14:45,090 --> 00:14:46,720
- Right.
- He doesn't sleep much...

320
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:47,920
- and keeps wandering around.
- He doesn't eat much either.

321
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:50,060
- Are you talking about Ugong?
- He's similar to Mokgye.

322
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:52,660
He and I actually share similar traits.

323
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:56,900
And he said that his wife and I share
a similar personality.

324
00:14:57,260 --> 00:14:58,500
- I see.
- Yes.

325
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:00,970
Is that why he stepped out?

326
00:15:01,170 --> 00:15:02,170
Both of them are so smart.

327
00:15:02,170 --> 00:15:04,710
He must feel like he's in his own home
when he's actually not.

328
00:15:04,710 --> 00:15:06,440
- Oh, that's why he stepped out.
- Because of me?

329
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:08,410
- He didn't want to be nagged.
- Suddenly, Ugong's actions make sense.

330
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:09,580
- You see...
- He keeps going out because of me?

331
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:12,110
My dad also keeps going out.

332
00:15:12,550 --> 00:15:15,220
Tell him to take out the trash
on his way out.

333
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:18,450
It's unbelievable.
I'll call him out on this.

334
00:15:18,550 --> 00:15:19,890
Will you tell him
to stop wandering around outside?

335
00:15:19,890 --> 00:15:21,360
Yes, I'll tell him to stay at home.

336
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,320
- See? They're all crowding over there.
- They're all over there.

337
00:15:23,490 --> 00:15:26,330
It became kind of an official activity.

338
00:15:26,330 --> 00:15:27,760
Ugong is not there, is he?

339
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,900
- He's not there.
- Where did he go?

340
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:35,070
Has any of you seen Ugong today?

341
00:15:35,070 --> 00:15:36,640
- Hello.
- It's occupied.

342
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:37,940
- Is Team Red using it?
- Has anyone seen Ugong?

343
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:40,010
- Ugong is in there?
- In the Community Center?

344
00:15:40,010 --> 00:15:42,040
- Is he switching to another team?
- What? Hold on a second.

345
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,410
Is Ugong in there?

346
00:15:43,410 --> 00:15:44,650
Then let's go in and check.

347
00:15:44,650 --> 00:15:46,110
Isn't it Maillard who's in there?

348
00:15:46,110 --> 00:15:47,810
Maybe both Ugong and Maillard are
in there.

349
00:15:47,810 --> 00:15:49,350
- He keeps... Check the inside.
- I saw Maillard going in there.

350
00:15:49,350 --> 00:15:51,050
- Just take a peek.
- For now...

351
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,320
You can use it now.

352
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,660
Let me talk to him for just a moment.

353
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:57,790
- Oh, Ugong is coming out of there.
- It's so suspicious.

354
00:15:58,990 --> 00:16:00,830
- I'll just talk to him for a moment.
- Okay.

355
00:16:01,230 --> 00:16:03,100
- Let me just talk to him briefly.
- Okay.

356
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,930
- I'll be back shortly.
- All right.

357
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,570
- Looks like they had some talk.
- Right.

358
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:10,840
From my perspective, Team Red...

359
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:12,110
- Hold on just a second.
- Sure.

360
00:16:12,210 --> 00:16:13,440
This is...

361
00:16:13,810 --> 00:16:15,910
the same situation we talked about
this morning, right?

362
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:18,950
- Yes.
- But right now, it seems a little...

363
00:16:19,110 --> 00:16:20,710
- That's not the case.
- It's not?

364
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,650
No. Nothing has changed.

365
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:27,420
From my perspective,
Team Gold hasn't shed any blood yet.

366
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,560
And I think that's why
the two teams feel differently.

367
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:31,860
In my opinion, Team Gold's issue is...

368
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,890
that they want to survive to the end...

369
00:16:33,890 --> 00:16:35,630
without shedding any blood...

370
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:37,700
and walk away with all the prize money.

371
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,100
Let's say we need to take out two people.

372
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:42,200
I can't just tell them,
"Take out two people..."

373
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:44,570
"and split
the remaining prize money evenly,"

374
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:46,910
"then we'll believe you're sincere."

375
00:16:46,910 --> 00:16:49,240
I can't just say that, you know.

376
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:50,540
- I'm not even the leader.
- Right.

377
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:53,480
Considering our current situation,

378
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:56,050
the scenario I have in mind
can't be achieved by using lives.

379
00:16:56,050 --> 00:16:59,550
I believe that a casting vote should hold
the power to completely eliminate someone.

380
00:16:59,550 --> 00:17:01,120
- We're just passing through.
- Okay.

381
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:04,730
But right now, it's already...

382
00:17:05,290 --> 00:17:06,830
So in this situation...

383
00:17:07,530 --> 00:17:09,730
I already told them I'd join your team...

384
00:17:09,730 --> 00:17:11,330
to help them win.

385
00:17:11,330 --> 00:17:13,300
They keep coming to check on us
because they're suspicious of me.

386
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:15,900
There's no reason we shouldn't hear
their conversation, is there?

387
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:17,940
- Exactly. There's no reason...
- That's why it's so suspicious.

388
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:19,070
we shouldn't hear their conversation.

389
00:17:19,070 --> 00:17:20,240
- Their conversation?
- Yes.

390
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,950
We don't have enough intel
to pinpoint what he's up to.

391
00:17:24,950 --> 00:17:26,410
And his relocation is
completely out of my hands.

392
00:17:26,410 --> 00:17:28,020
I have no authority to stop him.

393
00:17:28,020 --> 00:17:31,420
If he decides to leave this team,
he can leave us.

394
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:34,290
It's not that I'm suspicious of him.
I want him to share his decision with us.

395
00:17:34,290 --> 00:17:37,290
- He's not sharing his thoughts with us.
- That's true, yes.

396
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:39,560
If he's leaving,
we might as well take someone in too.

397
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:41,500
I mean, it'd be good for us
if someone from Team Red joins our team.

398
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:43,560
That's a given. I'm up
for taking in a member from Team Red.

399
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:44,560
- I'm definitely going to take him in.
- Right.

400
00:17:45,370 --> 00:17:46,670
Vector, can we talk to you for a second?

401
00:17:46,770 --> 00:17:47,770
- Me?
- Yes.

402
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:50,800
Don't have that sulky look on your face.

403
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:52,640
- Team Gold is over there, so...
- Oh, okay.

404
00:17:52,910 --> 00:17:55,280
- I'll go tell him to come when he's done.
- Seriously.

405
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:57,580
- When he's done...
- I'll say we won't go up there.

406
00:17:57,580 --> 00:18:00,180
I can't trust him 100 percent.
I'll trust him for now.

407
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:01,920
In my opinion,

408
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:04,280
Team Diamond doesn't have a spot for you.

409
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:06,150
- I can't move to your team?
- You can't move to our team.

410
00:18:06,150 --> 00:18:07,390
I'm telling you honestly.

411
00:18:07,590 --> 00:18:10,690
But there are ways for Team Gold to win.

412
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:13,860
I don't see many paths to victory for us.

413
00:18:14,060 --> 00:18:18,730
I said that
Team Gold would definitely need me...

414
00:18:18,870 --> 00:18:21,670
because I can keep an eye
on Team Diamond's resources.

415
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:25,440
- Right. But from our perspective,
- Yes.

416
00:18:26,470 --> 00:18:29,080
there needs to be some kind of benefit
we can offer you...

417
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:30,680
- There is.
- What is it?

418
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,150
You can start a war,

419
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:33,910
at a reasonable cost.

420
00:18:34,350 --> 00:18:36,750
Your team is already on thin ice.

421
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:38,320
So you're saying...

422
00:18:38,450 --> 00:18:39,720
if you can gain...

423
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:42,320
some more prize money through a war,

424
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,590
- you will vote for our currency?
- Absolutely.

425
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:47,130
But Team Diamond has already made me
that offer.

426
00:18:47,390 --> 00:18:50,430
Team Red also promised me
they'd start a war for me.

427
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:55,870
- But if Team Gold raises the stakes...
- But...

428
00:18:55,870 --> 00:18:57,640
- and goes to war,
- Yes.

429
00:18:57,940 --> 00:18:59,640
I might help them.

430
00:19:08,050 --> 00:19:09,450
That makes things very complicated.

431
00:19:12,650 --> 00:19:16,490
It's a 6-on-7 or 8-on-5 situation
right now.

432
00:19:16,690 --> 00:19:18,660
If 1 or 2 people get eliminated,

433
00:19:19,260 --> 00:19:20,990
the tables could turn.

434
00:19:20,990 --> 00:19:23,000
You must know this since you've played
a Majority Rules Game before.

435
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,700
Once you slightly cross the line,
the whole thing can change.

436
00:19:26,930 --> 00:19:27,930
Oh, there he is.

437
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:31,640
Okay.

438
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:33,340
That's a little...

439
00:19:34,270 --> 00:19:35,880
I'm just letting you know
in case you don't know.

440
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:37,010
- I understand for now.
- Okay.

441
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,850
One of my team members is here.
I should go now.

442
00:19:39,850 --> 00:19:40,850
All right.

443
00:19:40,850 --> 00:19:42,620
- Everyone is waiting for you.
- Right.

444
00:19:44,780 --> 00:19:47,350
It's so complicated.

445
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:50,060
We're going to split it evenly,

446
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:51,390
- so it doesn't matter to me.
- Nothing will change.

447
00:19:51,390 --> 00:19:52,430
- Leia.
- Yes?

448
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:54,290
Please trust other people.

449
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:56,160
This place made me who I am today.

450
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:58,170
- I used to trust others so easily.
- The boundaries have already been set.

451
00:19:58,170 --> 00:20:00,300
- All right. I get it.
- A boundary has already been...

452
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:01,500
formed like this.

453
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,800
In a way,
the safest place in the world right now...

454
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,640
is within Maillard's boundary.

455
00:20:08,810 --> 00:20:09,940
Now,

456
00:20:09,940 --> 00:20:12,980
a 4-on-1 alliance has been formed.

457
00:20:13,550 --> 00:20:16,420
(Maillard's complete victory plan
with the diamond alliance)

458
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:18,650
There are eight people left.

459
00:20:18,690 --> 00:20:19,790
It's 3, 3, 1, 1.

460
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:23,160
Open sesame.

461
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:24,990
We can make the request
at the same time, right?

462
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:27,730
To bring up the productivity,

463
00:20:27,790 --> 00:20:30,730
I wanted to use the Relocation Rule.

464
00:20:32,570 --> 00:20:35,400
Name the team you wish to relocate to.

465
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,540
- Team Blue.
- Team Blue.

466
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:38,870
- Team Blue.
- I will relocate to Team Blue.

467
00:20:38,910 --> 00:20:41,070
Paul of Team White...

468
00:20:41,070 --> 00:20:43,880
- has requested relocation to Team Blue.
- Yes!

469
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,950
Siseon of Team White...

470
00:20:45,950 --> 00:20:46,980
- has requested...
- Yes!

471
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:49,050
Izaha of Team Red...

472
00:20:49,050 --> 00:20:51,020
- has requested...
- Yes!

473
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:52,990
Donkey of Team Red...

474
00:20:52,990 --> 00:20:55,790
has requested relocation to Team Blue.

475
00:20:56,390 --> 00:20:58,430
This is going to be fun!

476
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,890
Paul of Team White...

477
00:21:00,990 --> 00:21:02,960
Siseon of Team White...

478
00:21:03,030 --> 00:21:05,070
Izaha of Team Red...

479
00:21:05,070 --> 00:21:07,030
Donkey of Team Red...

480
00:21:07,030 --> 00:21:09,270
has relocated to Team Blue.

481
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:11,540
Knock!

482
00:21:13,070 --> 00:21:17,340
Five people were sent
to the production facility.

483
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,410
When the production is over,

484
00:21:19,410 --> 00:21:21,010
we'll trade with Black right away...

485
00:21:21,010 --> 00:21:22,150
to purchase the skill.

486
00:21:22,150 --> 00:21:23,450
(Purchase Team White's skill
as soon as trading begins.)

487
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:27,720
We'll move our resources
through the Platform before a war happens.

488
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:30,190
(Move resources through the Platform
in case of a war.)

489
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:33,260
The members who went to Team Blue...

490
00:21:33,260 --> 00:21:35,860
will all move to Team Red.
All five of them.

491
00:21:35,860 --> 00:21:38,300
They can move multiple times.

492
00:21:39,130 --> 00:21:41,900
I'm here to issue Team White's currency.

493
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:44,470
Leia will stay in Team White.

494
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:46,510
She will go to war on her own
as Team White.

495
00:21:46,510 --> 00:21:48,170
(Team White will declare war
as a 1-person group.)

496
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:50,010
After that...

497
00:21:50,010 --> 00:21:51,710
This is when the move to Team Red happens.

498
00:21:51,780 --> 00:21:53,380
It's after the resources
have been distributed.

499
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:55,720
There's no announcement
for the distribution of resources,

500
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:57,350
but there are announcements
for relocations.

501
00:21:57,350 --> 00:21:59,520
If the relocation announcements...

502
00:21:59,850 --> 00:22:01,790
of the ones who went to do
productive activities happen first,

503
00:22:01,790 --> 00:22:04,520
- they will find it strange.
