1258
00:49:26,700 --> 00:49:29,130
About waging a war or not,
we can just vote for or against.

1259
00:49:29,130 --> 00:49:30,170
Mokgye is insisting...

1260
00:49:30,170 --> 00:49:31,670
- She wants to.
- that we should wage war today.

1261
00:49:31,670 --> 00:49:34,540
- We can vote.
- The thing is, if we wage war today,

1262
00:49:34,640 --> 00:49:35,810
it might become tricky...

1263
00:49:35,810 --> 00:49:37,540
- to negotiate after that.
- Right.

1264
00:49:37,710 --> 00:49:40,050
- So it's a matter of when to wage war?
- Exactly.

1265
00:49:40,050 --> 00:49:42,880
If you have a chance
to talk enough, do it.

1266
00:49:42,880 --> 00:49:44,680
If the conversation doesn't work,

1267
00:49:44,880 --> 00:49:46,450
then we can wage war as an option.

1268
00:49:46,450 --> 00:49:48,120
So I'm not saying
that we should never wage war.

1269
00:49:48,120 --> 00:49:49,720
If we should do it, let's do it tomorrow.
That's my opinion.

1270
00:49:49,820 --> 00:49:52,790
I feel like I have even less reason
to do that today.

1271
00:49:52,790 --> 00:49:54,760
I'm against doing it today.

1272
00:49:54,760 --> 00:49:58,760
I just want to make some kind
of change, whatever it may be.

1273
00:49:58,900 --> 00:50:01,500
I feel like nothing will change
unless we actually try.

1274
00:50:01,500 --> 00:50:05,440
"Let's give it a try.
Let's make a change."

1275
00:50:05,440 --> 00:50:06,640
Everyone agrees with that.

1276
00:50:06,640 --> 00:50:08,070
There's no one here
who disagrees with that.

1277
00:50:08,070 --> 00:50:12,710
We didn't know why things weren't working,
and now we finally know.

1278
00:50:12,810 --> 00:50:15,480
We only realized today
what the structural contradictions...

1279
00:50:15,550 --> 00:50:17,120
and limitations
are that make it impossible...

1280
00:50:17,120 --> 00:50:18,580
after looking at all the information
we had yesterday.

1281
00:50:18,720 --> 00:50:22,590
We've tried everything we could
to make it work, but we couldn't.

1282
00:50:23,190 --> 00:50:25,460
So I understand why you might say,
"Let's go to war."

1283
00:50:25,460 --> 00:50:28,990
But honestly, I find it really hard
to agree with that.

1284
00:50:29,090 --> 00:50:30,630
That doesn't mean
we shouldn't do anything.

1285
00:50:30,630 --> 00:50:31,900
So what should we do today?

1286
00:50:32,160 --> 00:50:34,430
In our current situation,
we also need to choose...

1287
00:50:34,430 --> 00:50:35,730
not to do certain things
because we simply can't do them.

1288
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:38,140
I believe that choosing not to act
is also a form of action.

1289
00:50:38,140 --> 00:50:40,570
- Understood.
- In the meantime,

1290
00:50:40,570 --> 00:50:42,270
if anyone wants to talk to someone,
I think that's fine.

1291
00:50:42,470 --> 00:50:45,440
But I think it's also okay...

1292
00:50:45,680 --> 00:50:50,050
to gently inform others
about our current situation.

1293
00:50:50,050 --> 00:50:52,620
Those who want to take a break
can go ahead and rest now.

1294
00:50:52,620 --> 00:50:55,720
Since the majority of us...

1295
00:50:56,150 --> 00:50:58,390
- are against going to war today anyway,
- I'm against doing it today.

1296
00:50:58,390 --> 00:51:00,290
we've decided not to do it.

1297
00:51:00,290 --> 00:51:03,190
I'll just tell Leia,
"What I mentioned before..."

1298
00:51:03,190 --> 00:51:05,360
"was simply one of the options..."

1299
00:51:05,360 --> 00:51:06,870
- "we were considering."
- Yes.

1300
00:51:07,470 --> 00:51:09,530
"We realized that this was the outcome
we could expect."

1301
00:51:09,530 --> 00:51:11,570
- I'll just say that.
- Okay.

1302
00:51:11,740 --> 00:51:13,040
Feel free to...

1303
00:51:22,980 --> 00:51:25,150
- I had nothing to say.
- Mokgye is coming.

1304
00:51:25,150 --> 00:51:27,220
- Mokgye is coming.
- Mokgye is coming.

1305
00:51:27,420 --> 00:51:28,550
Why aren't you guys eating?

1306
00:51:28,750 --> 00:51:29,850
- Us?
- Yes.

1307
00:51:29,850 --> 00:51:31,020
We don't have much of an appetite.

1308
00:51:31,020 --> 00:51:32,960
- Why not?
- Shouldn't you eat something, though?

1309
00:51:33,220 --> 00:51:35,160
Have you guys talked?

1310
00:51:35,160 --> 00:51:37,200
We have, but like I was worried about,

1311
00:51:37,200 --> 00:51:39,000
- we didn't come to a clear answer.
- I see.

1312
00:51:39,200 --> 00:51:41,970
Some people said they wanted
to communicate more with Team Gold.

1313
00:51:42,300 --> 00:51:43,870
- Anyway...
- Since this was something...

1314
00:51:43,870 --> 00:51:44,900
- we had only discussed among ourselves,
- Yes.

1315
00:51:44,900 --> 00:51:47,310
they had some questions
they wanted to ask.

1316
00:51:48,010 --> 00:51:51,710
So they thought it'd be a good idea
to talk things over...

1317
00:51:51,980 --> 00:51:55,210
with the other members of Team Gold
as well, and we were waiting.

1318
00:51:55,210 --> 00:51:56,580
But no one from your team
came over for the meal.

1319
00:51:56,580 --> 00:51:59,820
- If this proposal is accepted,
- Okay.

1320
00:52:00,150 --> 00:52:01,590
I'm willing to do whatever I can...

1321
00:52:01,590 --> 00:52:02,690
- No.
- to push it forward.

1322
00:52:02,690 --> 00:52:05,420
Instead of asking us to give you
a definite answer first,

1323
00:52:05,420 --> 00:52:06,660
if we want to make a commitment
to each other,

1324
00:52:06,660 --> 00:52:07,930
- Then I...
- you need to bring your team members.

1325
00:52:07,930 --> 00:52:09,760
Then I'll give you a definite answer...

1326
00:52:09,760 --> 00:52:12,300
on their behalf. We'll do it.

1327
00:52:12,330 --> 00:52:14,130
I'm not the leader right now, but...

1328
00:52:14,130 --> 00:52:15,930
- The leader has to come.
- What?

1329
00:52:16,570 --> 00:52:18,540
- This doesn't feel right.
- Yes. This is...

1330
00:52:18,540 --> 00:52:20,640
I understand you're trying hard, but...

1331
00:52:20,640 --> 00:52:22,810
- If you can't persuade your leader...
- Even if you give us a clear answer,

1332
00:52:22,810 --> 00:52:23,840
if the leader rejects it...

1333
00:52:23,840 --> 00:52:24,840
- and the negotiations fall apart,
- Right?

1334
00:52:24,840 --> 00:52:26,140
- Think about it.
- we'll be the ones getting screwed over.

1335
00:52:26,140 --> 00:52:27,380
Look. What if you came here
and finished the negotiations with us,

1336
00:52:27,380 --> 00:52:29,110
but then your leader
didn't accept the agreement?

1337
00:52:29,310 --> 00:52:31,180
In that case, I think the leader
should be replaced.

1338
00:52:31,180 --> 00:52:35,290
That's why we have
a leadership vote every morning.

1339
00:52:35,420 --> 00:52:39,060
I think a leader who can't represent
the will of the team should step down.

1340
00:52:39,790 --> 00:52:42,730
If even this proposal
can't be agreed upon,

1341
00:52:43,560 --> 00:52:45,460
I'm starting to feel like
Team Gold isn't going to win.

1342
00:52:45,460 --> 00:52:49,700
My expectations for Gold
are getting lower and lower,

1343
00:52:49,700 --> 00:52:52,270
and I'm increasingly starting to think
that it's going to be hard for you to win.

1344
00:52:52,270 --> 00:52:55,270
Because if your team can't even agree
on something as simple...

1345
00:52:55,270 --> 00:52:56,810
as having all your team members
come down together during lunch,

1346
00:52:57,910 --> 00:52:59,440
how are we supposed to discuss
anything with you?

1347
00:53:00,910 --> 00:53:03,450
In this situation,

1348
00:53:03,450 --> 00:53:06,350
unless you're saying that you want to
and join our team on your own,

1349
00:53:06,450 --> 00:53:08,450
I don't think you can represent
your team's position.

1350
00:53:08,450 --> 00:53:11,160
This feels like a conversation
between individuals,

1351
00:53:11,160 --> 00:53:13,530
not a conversation between representatives
of the two teams.

1352
00:53:13,690 --> 00:53:15,890
That means this conversation
won't affect either team's decisions.

1353
00:53:16,230 --> 00:53:17,730
We can discuss this again,

1354
00:53:17,730 --> 00:53:20,330
but there's no point in you
giving us a firm commitment here.

1355
00:53:21,430 --> 00:53:22,500
That's it.

1356
00:53:22,930 --> 00:53:26,240
I felt like if we just kept doing nothing,

1357
00:53:26,770 --> 00:53:29,940
then this situation
would basically end like this.

1358
00:53:30,040 --> 00:53:34,210
Honestly, I thought the existing residents
would probably just see us...

1359
00:53:34,280 --> 00:53:38,720
as the team that stays in their room
and never comes out.

1360
00:53:38,850 --> 00:53:41,720
It was frustrating to me
that we weren't even trying anything.

1361
00:53:41,920 --> 00:53:45,620
"Will this kind of silent protest
actually work here?"

1362
00:53:45,990 --> 00:53:47,530
I kept wondering.

1363
00:53:47,760 --> 00:53:49,590
And honestly,
I didn't like their approach.

1364
00:53:52,460 --> 00:53:53,670
This is so hard.

1365
00:54:02,610 --> 00:54:04,240
I'll be back soon.

1366
00:54:04,240 --> 00:54:06,640
I'll get some fresh air and see
if there's anyone around to talk to.

1367
00:54:14,790 --> 00:54:17,260
Ugong. Can we talk for a moment?

1368
00:54:17,790 --> 00:54:18,790
What is it?

1369
00:54:19,160 --> 00:54:21,730
- I talked with Maillard earlier.
- Okay.

1370
00:54:21,960 --> 00:54:25,130
They said I hadn't made a proposal
that was appealing enough to them.

1371
00:54:25,560 --> 00:54:26,900
- That's what I thought.
- Yes.

1372
00:54:26,900 --> 00:54:30,470
I really want everyone to come together
and discuss this as a group.

1373
00:54:30,570 --> 00:54:32,200
I genuinely mean that.

1374
00:54:32,200 --> 00:54:34,410
You keep talking to me 1-on-1,

1375
00:54:34,410 --> 00:54:36,310
and I'm doing the same.

1376
00:54:36,310 --> 00:54:39,680
Instead of continuing like this,
I think we should all get together...

1377
00:54:39,740 --> 00:54:43,920
and keep trying to work something out.

1378
00:54:43,920 --> 00:54:47,550
Even if it turns into a complete mess,

1379
00:54:48,190 --> 00:54:50,020
even if we have to get down in the mud,

1380
00:54:50,020 --> 00:54:51,690
I think we need to stir things up
at least once.

1381
00:54:51,690 --> 00:54:55,560
You're right, but we need to think
about how we're going to stir things up.

1382
00:54:55,560 --> 00:54:56,860
Why do we need to think about that?

1383
00:54:56,860 --> 00:54:58,700
Let's just do it
and put in a little effort first.

1384
00:54:58,700 --> 00:55:01,400
- Because right now, we...
- But we need to have a way...

1385
00:55:01,400 --> 00:55:02,900
- to stir things up.
- Okay. Then...

1386
00:55:02,900 --> 00:55:03,900
Are you saying we should just cause chaos?

1387
00:55:03,900 --> 00:55:05,840
No. That's not what I mean.

1388
00:55:05,940 --> 00:55:07,770
I'm saying that Team Red and our team
should come together...

1389
00:55:07,770 --> 00:55:10,340
and propose giving them 80 percent
of the prize money.

1390
00:55:13,980 --> 00:55:15,450
Let's at least make an offer like that.

1391
00:55:17,020 --> 00:55:18,180
Let's just give it a try.

1392
00:55:18,180 --> 00:55:21,190
Why are we just sitting here doing nothing
and saying it won't work?

1393
00:55:21,190 --> 00:55:22,350
- But...
- Okay.

1394
00:55:23,350 --> 00:55:25,990
Let's just give it a try
and see how it goes.

1395
00:55:28,830 --> 00:55:31,760
Instead of saying,
"This isn't going to work. It's all lies."

1396
00:55:31,760 --> 00:55:33,830
"We're not doing it,"

1397
00:55:34,030 --> 00:55:35,400
we should at least give it a try...

1398
00:55:35,400 --> 00:55:37,570
and see for ourselves
whether it really doesn't work...

1399
00:55:37,570 --> 00:55:38,570
or whether we're wrong.

1400
00:55:42,240 --> 00:55:43,240
Then...

1401
00:55:45,380 --> 00:55:47,780
I agree with that for now.

1402
00:55:48,280 --> 00:55:50,650
Why don't you bring it up
with the others...

1403
00:55:50,650 --> 00:55:54,290
and get their official approval?

1404
00:55:54,420 --> 00:55:56,720
- I...
- It's so frustrating...

1405
00:55:56,720 --> 00:55:59,490
that I'm always in a position
where I have to get everyone's permission.

1406
00:55:59,720 --> 00:56:03,330
Can't we all just come together
and talk to them?

1407
00:56:03,330 --> 00:56:05,060
If we all get together,
we won't be able to reach a consensus.

1408
00:56:05,060 --> 00:56:06,560
Why can't we all get together?

1409
00:56:06,560 --> 00:56:10,300
- I'm not saying we can't.
- They want to talk to all of us.

1410
00:56:10,300 --> 00:56:13,910
What I mean is,
I want all of us to come together...

1411
00:56:13,910 --> 00:56:15,810
- and try to work something out.
- I mean...

1412
00:56:15,810 --> 00:56:18,240
Why don't you gather
our team's opinions...

1413
00:56:18,240 --> 00:56:20,680
and present our official position to them?
That'll work.

1414
00:56:21,980 --> 00:56:25,420
- I think...
- But we'll be voting.

1415
00:56:25,580 --> 00:56:27,990
Let's say I put forward a proposal.

1416
00:56:27,990 --> 00:56:29,950
"What do you think about splitting
the prize money 80 to 20 with Red?"

1417
00:56:29,950 --> 00:56:31,390
Then they will give their opinions.

1418
00:56:31,390 --> 00:56:33,390
And then we'll just say,
"No, that won't work. This won't work."

1419
00:56:33,390 --> 00:56:35,430
"This will happen."

1420
00:56:35,430 --> 00:56:37,330
"I've thought about it,
and for these reasons,"

1421
00:56:37,330 --> 00:56:39,430
"they must've already done the math."

1422
00:56:39,630 --> 00:56:41,570
- That's what we'll do.
- I get what you mean.

1423
00:56:41,570 --> 00:56:43,970
We keep assuming it won't work
without even trying.

1424
00:56:44,200 --> 00:56:46,370
Who knows?
If we make the proposal to them now,

1425
00:56:46,370 --> 00:56:47,610
and the situation changes later...

1426
00:56:47,610 --> 00:56:50,210
and they come back saying, "We talked
about this before. We'd like to do it."

1427
00:56:50,210 --> 00:56:52,840
Then we can take that opportunity.

1428
00:56:53,240 --> 00:56:57,010
We need to push against the situation
and somehow make a change.

1429
00:56:57,010 --> 00:57:00,180
There has to be a crack for us
to find a way in.

1430
00:57:00,390 --> 00:57:03,790
But we analyze every possible situation
and say, "It won't work."

1431
00:57:03,990 --> 00:57:06,760
- That's why we're stuck.
- Okay.

1432
00:57:07,160 --> 00:57:08,730
I think we need to at least try something.

1433
00:57:08,730 --> 00:57:10,760
- Even if we lose,
- I get it.

1434
00:57:10,760 --> 00:57:13,300
- we have to try something.
- Okay.

1435
00:57:13,530 --> 00:57:15,100
If that doesn't work,
we can even make a more drastic offer,

1436
00:57:15,100 --> 00:57:17,540
keeping in mind
that they might betray us later.

1437
00:57:17,640 --> 00:57:21,210
We could say, "We'll add another 100
to the offer. Let's split it 150 to 50."

1438
00:57:21,210 --> 00:57:22,340
Even if they demand an even bigger share,

1439
00:57:22,340 --> 00:57:24,410
we could say, "Okay. What matters is..."

1440
00:57:24,410 --> 00:57:26,080
"that we survive and win."

1441
00:57:26,080 --> 00:57:27,980
- I get it.
- "It's better for us to introduce gold."

1442
00:57:27,980 --> 00:57:31,880
"We can worry about the rest later.
We'll give you 180 in total."

1443
00:57:32,020 --> 00:57:33,750
We need to at least
make an offer like that.

1444
00:57:33,750 --> 00:57:35,420
But our teammates will say,

1445
00:57:35,420 --> 00:57:36,650
- I get it.
- "It's meaningless."

1446
00:57:36,650 --> 00:57:39,490
I get it. Please calm down.
I understand why you're mad.

1447
00:57:39,490 --> 00:57:40,930
They always look for...

1448
00:57:40,930 --> 00:57:43,030
- some kind of meaning.
- Gosh, you startled me.

1449
00:57:43,290 --> 00:57:45,460
I get it. But who's looking for meaning?

1450
00:57:45,460 --> 00:57:49,000
I mean, they always say,
"What's the point of this?"

1451
00:57:49,700 --> 00:57:52,740
But then what's the point
of what we're doing right now?

1452
00:57:53,370 --> 00:57:54,440
This is driving me nuts.

1453
00:57:56,310 --> 00:57:58,140
I get your point, but...

1454
00:57:58,410 --> 00:58:01,080
I'm sorry.

1455
00:58:01,580 --> 00:58:03,780
I was trying my best,

1456
00:58:04,320 --> 00:58:07,450
but I guess that wasn't enough.
All right. I'm sorry.

1457
00:58:10,760 --> 00:58:11,790
All right.

1458
00:58:12,090 --> 00:58:13,320
This is driving me crazy.

1459
00:58:14,860 --> 00:58:16,360
It's okay.

1460
00:58:16,360 --> 00:58:19,230
We still have time. Let's work hard.

1461
00:58:19,230 --> 00:58:20,700
I'm sorry.

1462
00:58:20,700 --> 00:58:24,070
It's because I've also had a lot
building up over the past few days.

1463
00:58:24,070 --> 00:58:26,770
- You might be feeling pessimistic now,
- So... Yes.

1464
00:58:26,770 --> 00:58:28,610
- I need to get over it too.
- But even if things look pessimistic now,

1465
00:58:28,610 --> 00:58:29,910
that doesn't mean...

1466
00:58:29,910 --> 00:58:32,010
- they're going to stay that way.
- But the thing is... I'm sorry.

1467
00:58:32,140 --> 00:58:34,450
Anyway,
I totally understand what you mean.

1468
00:58:34,750 --> 00:58:35,880
You should become the leader tomorrow.

1469
00:58:35,910 --> 00:58:38,420
We didn't even have time
to change leaders today...

1470
00:58:38,420 --> 00:58:39,650
because you were out.

1471
00:58:39,650 --> 00:58:41,190
I was telling Maetel and Luna,

1472
00:58:41,190 --> 00:58:42,420
"I want to become the leader tomorrow."

1473
00:58:42,420 --> 00:58:43,990
- "Please vote for me."
- You were?

1474
00:58:43,990 --> 00:58:45,660
But you weren't even there.

1475
00:58:45,660 --> 00:58:48,030
I'm sorry. I...

1476
00:58:48,030 --> 00:58:49,930
I missed that opportunity too.

1477
00:58:50,600 --> 00:58:52,260
- Gosh, it's so frustrating.
- Sorry.

1478
00:58:52,260 --> 00:58:54,300
I'm just trying to do something.

1479
00:58:57,400 --> 00:59:00,610
- I get it.
- Let's go back to my suggestion.

1480
00:59:00,610 --> 00:59:03,510
First, let's all get together
with Team Red...

1481
00:59:03,710 --> 00:59:05,180
and talk things through.

1482
00:59:05,210 --> 00:59:06,780
- All of us?
- Yes.

1483
00:59:06,780 --> 00:59:09,550
- I mean... Let's do that.
- That's all I'm asking for.

1484
00:59:09,910 --> 00:59:11,920
Okay. I'll tell them.

1485
00:59:11,920 --> 00:59:14,820
- I'll go and talk to them.
- No. Don't say that you'll do it.

1486
00:59:14,820 --> 00:59:16,490
- Let's go together and talk.
- Okay. Let's go together.

1487
00:59:16,490 --> 00:59:18,720
Please. That's my wish.
Just do this one thing for me.

1488
00:59:18,720 --> 00:59:20,730
- Okay. I'll do it.
- Okay.

1489
00:59:20,930 --> 00:59:23,460
- Can we all talk...
- Yes.

1490
