You're going to turn this offer down...

1739
01:10:35,830 --> 01:10:37,770
just because
you spent five days with them?

1740
01:10:37,770 --> 01:10:39,740
But are you making this offer...

1741
01:10:39,740 --> 01:10:42,270
after you've all reached an agreement?

1742
01:10:42,270 --> 01:10:43,710
No, this was just my idea.

1743
01:10:43,710 --> 01:10:44,880
You're just throwing it out there?

1744
01:10:44,880 --> 01:10:46,710
- If I may...
- Go ahead.

1745
01:10:46,710 --> 01:10:48,310
I would like to support her.

1746
01:10:48,310 --> 01:10:50,850
Okay, Ugong is on board.

1747
01:10:50,850 --> 01:10:52,950
I guess you came to talk with us...

1748
01:10:52,950 --> 01:10:55,790
because it'll take too long
to talk among yourselves.

1749
01:10:56,590 --> 01:10:57,590
What are we up to now?

1750
01:10:57,590 --> 01:10:59,860
(Maillard arrived after the trade.)

1751
01:11:00,690 --> 01:11:02,690
- Should I get another umbrella?
- Thanks.

1752
01:11:03,060 --> 01:11:04,560
- It's pouring out here.
- Right.

1753
01:11:04,560 --> 01:11:06,430
It's showering suddenly.

1754
01:11:06,430 --> 01:11:08,870
I'll head inside for a while
since it's raining so much.

1755
01:11:08,870 --> 01:11:10,770
You should stay.

1756
01:11:10,770 --> 01:11:12,100
No, I'll go with you.

1757
01:11:12,100 --> 01:11:13,100
We'll go together.

1758
01:11:13,100 --> 01:11:15,340
What is she trying to do?

1759
01:11:15,340 --> 01:11:17,370
There's nothing we can do right now.

1760
01:11:17,370 --> 01:11:19,210
But we still need to reach an agreement.

1761
01:11:19,210 --> 01:11:20,440
This is so sudden.

1762
01:11:20,880 --> 01:11:22,650
We don't know how many people...

1763
01:11:22,650 --> 01:11:24,180
- like that offer or don't.
- Right.

1764
01:11:24,180 --> 01:11:27,380
She can't just bulldoze her way
into this without talking to us.

1765
01:11:27,550 --> 01:11:30,590
It makes those four hours of us
talking here meaningless.

1766
01:11:30,590 --> 01:11:33,020
I wanted to lay low for the day...

1767
01:11:33,020 --> 01:11:34,930
and let her talk on her own.

1768
01:11:34,930 --> 01:11:37,290
Then I wanted to deliver a blow tomorrow,

1769
01:11:37,290 --> 01:11:38,630
but now it's over.

1770
01:11:38,630 --> 01:11:40,360
Now, we won't have moves to make tomorrow.

1771
01:11:40,360 --> 01:11:43,470
Our plan was to wait for another day.

1772
01:11:43,470 --> 01:11:44,940
- Yes, for tomorrow.
- Exactly.

1773
01:11:44,940 --> 01:11:46,370
We were going to look for a chance.

1774
01:11:46,370 --> 01:11:48,440
But Mokgye thinks differently.

1775
01:11:48,440 --> 01:11:51,780
She thinks we need to step up
and try anything in this situation.

1776
01:11:51,780 --> 01:11:54,750
- But...
- She's entitled to her own opinions,

1777
01:11:54,750 --> 01:11:57,010
but she can't present
that idea like it was the team's.

1778
01:11:57,010 --> 01:11:58,220
She didn't say that.

1779
01:11:58,220 --> 01:12:00,220
We were all standing next to her.

1780
01:12:00,220 --> 01:12:03,690
I agree with you on that, Reboot.

1781
01:12:03,690 --> 01:12:06,020
But I told her she has my support.

1782
01:12:06,020 --> 01:12:09,360
I'm trying to say
that we must have grounds.

1783
01:12:09,360 --> 01:12:11,660
Why is she going against
what we all talked about together?

1784
01:12:11,660 --> 01:12:14,230
We thought we had
all reached an agreement,

1785
01:12:14,230 --> 01:12:16,630
but Mokgye never agreed to it.

1786
01:12:16,630 --> 01:12:19,740
I think she wants to try out her idea now.

1787
01:12:19,740 --> 01:12:21,140
She should've done that individually.

1788
01:12:21,140 --> 01:12:22,670
We're bound as a team,
so she has no choice.

1789
01:12:22,670 --> 01:12:24,270
I think she was frustrated.

1790
01:12:24,270 --> 01:12:26,180
She wanted to try something on her own,

1791
01:12:26,180 --> 01:12:27,610
but when she brought it up,

1792
01:12:27,610 --> 01:12:29,980
we turned it down
for this and that reason.

1793
01:12:29,980 --> 01:12:31,720
- But this sort of behavior...
- Yes?

1794
01:12:31,720 --> 01:12:34,650
- makes things difficult internally.
- You're right.

1795
01:12:34,650 --> 01:12:36,850
But please let this one slide.

1796
01:12:36,850 --> 01:12:40,490
Reboot was upset
she spoke about something...

1797
01:12:40,490 --> 01:12:42,060
that wasn't agreed upon as a team.

1798
01:12:42,060 --> 01:12:45,000
One side is focusing on the procedure,

1799
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:47,730
but the other side wants to take action.

1800
01:12:47,730 --> 01:12:50,900
Yet, we're all in the same team,
so I'm torn.

1801
01:12:50,900 --> 01:12:53,770
But regarding the issue, I thought...

1802
01:12:53,770 --> 01:12:57,140
Mokgye's impulsive decision
to break the status quo...

1803
01:12:57,140 --> 01:12:58,940
was vaild.

1804
01:12:58,940 --> 01:13:01,810
Maillard, I'll summarize things for you.

1805
01:13:01,810 --> 01:13:05,950
Mokgye wanted to
break through this situation,

1806
01:13:05,950 --> 01:13:08,620
and she offered
to share 80 percent of their gold.

1807
01:13:08,620 --> 01:13:11,020
And we should make a blood alliance.

1808
01:13:11,690 --> 01:13:13,490
Please adopt me as your daughter.

1809
01:13:13,490 --> 01:13:15,560
Or how about them?

1810
01:13:15,560 --> 01:13:17,530
But you've never responded
to our offers...

1811
01:13:17,530 --> 01:13:19,500
with sincerity before.

1812
01:13:19,500 --> 01:13:23,000
I thought those misunderstandings...

1813
01:13:23,000 --> 01:13:25,340
and the dragging conversation
were the problem.

1814
01:13:25,800 --> 01:13:27,600
Anyway, that's our offer.

1815
01:13:27,600 --> 01:13:29,470
I'd like for you to give us an answer now.

1816
01:13:29,470 --> 01:13:32,640
But we need to talk to the other team.

1817
01:13:32,640 --> 01:13:34,580
You called us first,

1818
01:13:34,580 --> 01:13:38,010
but they're grilling me
about giving you the diamonds.

1819
01:13:38,010 --> 01:13:39,920
I'm stuck between two teams.

1820
01:13:39,920 --> 01:13:41,250
I'm being questioned by White,

1821
01:13:41,250 --> 01:13:43,990
and now Gold wants
to make a blood alliance.

1822
01:13:44,290 --> 01:13:46,090
But that's just what Red is right now.

1823
01:13:46,090 --> 01:13:47,290
- It can't be helped.
- But if you think differently,

1824
01:13:47,290 --> 01:13:48,990
- any team that sides with you...
- Right, it's up to us.

1825
01:13:48,990 --> 01:13:50,230
gets to win this.

1826
01:13:50,230 --> 01:13:51,330
- Really?
- Yes.

1827
01:13:51,330 --> 01:13:52,330
Then why are you pressuring us?

1828
01:13:52,330 --> 01:13:54,560
- Red is definitely winning.
- Then we...

1829
01:13:54,560 --> 01:13:55,870
- offer 80 percent...
- Yesterday, we...

1830
01:13:55,870 --> 01:13:58,340
We said we were supporting Gold yesterday.

1831
01:13:58,340 --> 01:14:00,700
- You said nothing yesterday!
- But that was...

1832
01:14:00,700 --> 01:14:02,340
And now you want to make a blood alliance?

1833
01:14:02,340 --> 01:14:04,880
I already offered to be your adopted son!

1834
01:14:05,340 --> 01:14:07,080
Now you want to be our daughter?

1835
01:14:07,080 --> 01:14:09,350
I already did this yesterday!

1836
01:14:09,350 --> 01:14:10,810
- This was me!
- I...

1837
01:14:10,810 --> 01:14:12,480
- Please get up.
- Well...

1838
01:14:12,480 --> 01:14:14,580
- Stand up.
- That...

1839
01:14:14,580 --> 01:14:15,890
That was really...

1840
01:14:15,890 --> 01:14:18,360
a misjudgment on my part.

1841
01:14:18,360 --> 01:14:20,390
It's not too late for you to be adopted.

1842
01:14:22,160 --> 01:14:23,930
- We...
- Then...

1843
01:14:23,930 --> 01:14:25,560
are you talking about relocation?

1844
01:14:25,560 --> 01:14:27,800
What are you offering exactly?

1845
01:14:27,800 --> 01:14:29,770
An exchange of one person each.

1846
01:14:29,770 --> 01:14:31,770
Who are we exchanging?

1847
01:14:31,770 --> 01:14:33,140
It doesn't matter.

1848
01:14:33,140 --> 01:14:35,340
- I'd like to go, honestly.
- Yes?

1849
01:14:35,340 --> 01:14:37,440
I've wanted to work
with you for a while now.

1850
01:14:37,440 --> 01:14:38,480
Then Ugong will relocate to our team.

1851
01:14:38,480 --> 01:14:40,780
What's going to happen
based on these conditions?

1852
01:14:40,780 --> 01:14:41,850
A blood alliance.

1853
01:14:41,850 --> 01:14:45,950
We want reassurance that
you'll choose Gold at the end.

1854
01:14:45,950 --> 01:14:49,520
Then we promise you 80 percent.

1855
01:14:50,150 --> 01:14:52,620
- Eighty percent of your gold?
- Yes.

1856
01:14:52,620 --> 01:14:53,620
Exactly.

1857
01:14:59,130 --> 01:15:00,130
Okay.

1858
01:15:01,770 --> 01:15:04,100
I'm intrigued.

1859
01:15:04,100 --> 01:15:06,640
This is an offer you can't refuse.

1860
01:15:06,640 --> 01:15:08,670
But during negotiations,

1861
01:15:08,670 --> 01:15:11,640
it's best for you to have counteroffers.

1862
01:15:11,640 --> 01:15:13,240
That's why our offer is appealing to you.

1863
01:15:13,240 --> 01:15:15,410
When they hear we're friendly,

1864
01:15:15,410 --> 01:15:18,050
other teams might offer you a bigger cut.

1865
01:15:18,050 --> 01:15:21,080
Either way, Team Red gets the prize money,
no matter what.

1866
01:15:21,080 --> 01:15:23,750
The question is how much you'll get.

1867
01:15:23,750 --> 01:15:25,360
You might have to share with them.

1868
01:15:25,360 --> 01:15:26,460
But since we're offering 80 percent,

1869
01:15:26,460 --> 01:15:29,530
they might offer 90 percent in return.

1870
01:15:29,830 --> 01:15:32,630
Whatever the case,
this isn't a bad deal for you.

1871
01:15:32,960 --> 01:15:36,470
And we're being open about that.

1872
01:15:39,870 --> 01:15:41,300
I don't think I can
give you an answer right now.

1873
01:15:41,300 --> 01:15:43,340
They need to check with Reboot too.

1874
01:15:43,340 --> 01:15:46,080
- No, it's...
- Reboot will be okay.

1875
01:15:46,080 --> 01:15:49,180
It's not just that. He's the leader.

1876
01:15:49,180 --> 01:15:51,050
- He has a say...
- It's just one vote.

1877
01:15:51,180 --> 01:15:52,220
He's alone.

1878
01:15:52,220 --> 01:15:55,320
Our official decision is to go with this.

1879
01:15:55,320 --> 01:15:57,450
- With four votes, it's official.
- Yes.

1880
01:15:57,450 --> 01:15:59,560
- All right.
- Give us some time.

1881
01:15:59,560 --> 01:16:01,590
We can't really decide anything right now.

1882
01:16:01,590 --> 01:16:02,890
- Right.
- Come back later.

1883
01:16:02,890 --> 01:16:04,290
Just a moment.

1884
01:16:04,290 --> 01:16:08,000
- I hope you make a good decision.
- We won't keep you waiting.

1885
01:16:08,200 --> 01:16:10,170
Thanks for the offer.

1886
01:16:10,170 --> 01:16:11,500
Thank you.

1887
01:16:11,500 --> 01:16:13,670
I have a question.

1888
01:16:13,670 --> 01:16:16,270
- When you said 80 percent...
- Yes?

1889
01:16:16,270 --> 01:16:18,280
- I was...
- Is that from now?

1890
01:16:18,280 --> 01:16:19,280
- Or from the final?
- No, but...

1891
01:16:19,280 --> 01:16:20,380
eighty percent of what we have now.

1892
01:16:20,380 --> 01:16:21,780
Was that number agreed upon?

1893
01:16:21,780 --> 01:16:22,780
No.

1894
01:16:23,580 --> 01:16:25,820
- Actually...
- Why did you bring up a number?

1895
01:16:25,820 --> 01:16:27,720
- Reboot told me...
- Yes.

1896
01:16:27,720 --> 01:16:28,920
- he wasn't happy with this.
- Because of the percentage.

1897
01:16:28,920 --> 01:16:30,520
I was a little flustered too.

1898
01:16:30,520 --> 01:16:31,920
But it's a conversation starter.

1899
01:16:31,920 --> 01:16:33,690
It's 80 percent of our gold now,

1900
01:16:33,690 --> 01:16:35,030
but I think...

1901
01:16:35,690 --> 01:16:38,560
- Let's go in first.
- I think we can talk to them later.

1902
01:16:39,000 --> 01:16:41,260
So we give them
80 percent of the valuation now.

1903
01:16:41,260 --> 01:16:42,770
- If we issue more gold,
- Yes, 80 percent of now.

1904
01:16:42,770 --> 01:16:44,370
- the valuation will drop.
- Yes, we can issue more.

1905
01:16:44,370 --> 01:16:46,370
But if we issue gold after this,

1906
01:16:46,370 --> 01:16:47,540
we'd be betraying them.

1907
01:16:47,540 --> 01:16:48,940
I'm fine with 80 percent.

1908
01:16:48,940 --> 01:16:50,140
Let's see if they take our offer.

1909
01:16:50,140 --> 01:16:52,380
If they don't even accept
this amazing offer,

1910
01:16:52,380 --> 01:16:54,280
we'll think of the next step.

1911
01:16:54,840 --> 01:16:57,910
We have nothing without change now!

1912
01:16:57,910 --> 01:17:00,680
That's why I made an extreme decision.

1913
01:17:00,680 --> 01:17:01,920
I'll take responsibility.

1914
01:17:01,920 --> 01:17:04,720
I won't take the prize money.

1915
01:17:04,720 --> 01:17:07,020
I'm guessing the problem is
with the ratio.

1916
01:17:07,020 --> 01:17:08,360
I won't take my cut.

1917
01:17:08,360 --> 01:17:10,860
This isn't about the prize.

1918
01:17:11,330 --> 01:17:13,160
We're in a team here.

1919
01:17:13,160 --> 01:17:15,370
I understand you might be upset.

1920
01:17:15,370 --> 01:17:17,000
It's not about feelings either.

1921
01:17:17,000 --> 01:17:18,970
It might've been a miscommunication,

1922
01:17:18,970 --> 01:17:20,900
but Ugong first came up to us...

1923
01:17:20,900 --> 01:17:22,570
and asked us to just listen to
what you had to say.

1924
01:17:22,570 --> 01:17:23,940
That's why I went.

1925
01:17:23,940 --> 01:17:26,440
But you already decided on
a percentage of 80...

1926
01:17:26,440 --> 01:17:28,450
and made it seem like an official offer.

1927
01:17:28,450 --> 01:17:30,250
If I'd known that, I wouldn't have gone.

1928
01:17:30,250 --> 01:17:32,920
It's been only five days...

1929
01:17:32,920 --> 01:17:34,920
since we got here.

1930
01:17:34,920 --> 01:17:38,290
And I couldn't stand
the thought of not doing anything...

1931
01:17:38,290 --> 01:17:39,920
during our remaining time here.

1932
01:17:39,920 --> 01:17:41,420
That's why I already said
those who think so...

1933
01:17:41,420 --> 01:17:44,130
can do whatever you can individually.

1934
01:17:44,130 --> 01:17:46,130
But we really needed a change.

1935
01:17:46,130 --> 01:17:48,160
Yes, we know. We've talked about it.

1936
01:17:48,160 --> 01:17:49,970
But to bring about change,

1937
01:17:49,970 --> 01:17:52,740
we need to make impulsive decisions.

1938
01:17:52,740 --> 01:17:54,040
Otherwise, it'll be the same.

1939
01:17:54,040 --> 01:17:57,570
You understand
we're not part of your own team, Mokgye.

1940
01:17:57,570 --> 01:17:58,880
- Of course.
- Right?

1941
01:17:58,880 --> 01:18:00,280
- Then...
- I'm just a member.

1942
01:18:00,280 --> 01:18:01,980
We reached
a decision not to do anything...

1943
01:18:01,980 --> 01:18:04,550
through a lot of debate and conversation.

1944
01:18:04,550 --> 01:18:06,050
Things are bad as is.

1945
01:18:06,050 --> 01:18:07,780
Did you really have to make things harder?

1946
01:18:07,780 --> 01:18:10,090
Not taking action
would've made things harder.

1947
01:18:10,090 --> 01:18:11,390
- So...
- I'm not against taking action.

1948
01:18:11,390 --> 01:18:13,160
- Yes. But I think...
- There is a process to this...

1949
01:18:13,160 --> 01:18:14,960
Could I step in for a second?

1950
01:18:14,960 --> 01:18:17,130
I understand everything you've said.

1951
01:18:17,130 --> 01:18:20,000
There is the issue of the procedure,

1952
01:18:20,000 --> 01:18:22,570
and the ratio was a bit of a gamble.

1953
01:18:22,570 --> 01:18:25,140
This is how I took this.

1954
01:18:25,140 --> 01:18:29,110
We didn't get to reappoint
the leader because I wasn't here.

1955
01:18:29,110 --> 01:18:32,580
I think Mokgye wanted
to be the leader too.

1956
01:18:32,580 --> 01:18:34,810
I do feel bad to Reboot for saying this,

1957
01:18:34,810 --> 01:18:36,550
but I supported Mokgye...

1958
01:18:36,550 --> 01:18:40,980
as a way to start tomorrow a bit early.

1959
01:18:40,980 --> 01:18:42,420
This is a survival show.

1960
01:18:42,420 --> 01:18:44,720
It'll be great
to have everything by procedure.

1961
01:18:44,720 --> 01:18:47,660
But in this situation,
we have to play it by ear...

1962
01:18:47,660 --> 01:18:49,530
and respond to a sudden action...

1963
01:18:49,530 --> 01:18:51,960
from time to time.

1964
01:18:51,960 --> 01:18:53,530
I'd like to say something.

1965
01:18:53,530 --> 01:18:55,300
Things were already bad.

1966
01:18:55,300 --> 01:18:57,670
But acting on her own
without talking to us first...

1967
01:18:57,670 --> 01:19:00,170
was a mistake on Mokgye's part,
and she admitted it too.

1968
01:19:00,170 --> 01:19:02,970
What I don't want is
our team to split into two.

1969
01:19:03,370 --> 01:19:05,310
When we're divided,

1970
01:19:05,310 --> 01:19:07,410
we're going to start arguing.

1971
01:19:07,410 --> 01:19:09,250
It'll be like who's on Reboot's side,

1972
01:19:09,250 --> 01:19:10,750
and who's on Mokgye's side.

1973
01:19:10,750 --> 01:19:12,480
And if we start...

1974
01:19:12,480 --> 01:19:14,980
splitting up into groups as a team,

1975
01:19:14,980 --> 01:19:16,550
it'll ultimately come back to bite us.

1976
01:19:16,550 --> 01:19:18,220
I want to move on to the next step.

1977
01:19:19,160 --> 01:19:21,560
So all we do is wait for the moment?

1978
01:19:21,560 --> 01:19:22,590
There's nothing we can do?

1979
01:19:22,590 --> 01:19:26,160
Paul of Team Blue
has relocated to Team Red.

1980
01:19:26,630 --> 01:19:30,570
Paul, please go to your dormitory
within an hour.

1981
01:19:31,630 --> 01:19:33,770
- They're turning our offer down.
- Right.

1982
01:19:33,770 --> 01:19:34,900
This is...

1983
01:19:34,900 --> 01:19:37,040
Paul of Team Blue
has relocated to Team Red.

1984
01:19:37,510 --> 01:19:38,580
This is interesting.

1985
01:19:38,580 --> 01:19:40,310
So they're turning it down.

1986
01:19:40,310 --> 01:19:41,750
Even an offer of 80 percent!

1987
01:19:41,750 --> 01:19:43,510
But why? What did they offer?

1988
01:19:43,510 --> 01:19:47,520
Staying inside right now is really bad.

1989
01:19:47,520 --> 01:19:50,020
The other teams are communicating...

1990
01:19:50,020 --> 01:19:51,290
to convince each other...

1991
01:19:51,290 --> 01:19:52,560
and make offers.

1992
01:19:52,560 --> 01:19:54,890
- It doesn't matter now.
- Then let's go over to Red.

1993
01:19:54,890 --> 01:19:56,930
We can ask them...

1994
01:19:56,930 --> 01:19:58,130
why they made this decision.

1995
01:19:58,130 --> 01:19:59,960
Siseon of Team Blue...

1996
01:19:59,960 --> 01:20:02,130
- has relocated to Team Red.
- Who?

1997
01:20:02,570 --> 01:20:04,070
Siseon is going to Red too.

1998
01:20:04,630 --> 01:20:06,340
So they're bonding like this.

1999
01:20:06,340 --> 01:20:09,270
They're doing exactly
what we offered them.

2000
01:20:09,270 --> 01:20:11,140
They might've gotten a higher cut.

2001
01:20:11,270 --> 01:20:12,310
That's true.

2002
01:20:12,310 --> 01:20:14,580
- Didn't you see this coming?
- No, we did.

2003
01:20:14,580 --> 01:20:16,510
- This was to be expected.
- Yes.

2004
01:20:16,510 --> 01:20:19,220
It's true that there's been a change...

2005
01:20:19,220 --> 01:20:21,080
because we went out and took action.

2006
01:20:21,080 --> 01:20:23,490
We have to keep stirring the pot...

2007
01:20:23,490 --> 01:20:25,660
to find a crack for us to enter through.

2008
01:20:25,660 --> 01:20:28,660
- What if it brings them closer?
- That could happen.

2009
01:20:28,830 --> 01:20:31,800
But I think shaking things up is
needed to find the fissure.

2010
01:20:31,960 --> 01:20:33,330
I disagree.

2011
01:20:36,370 --> 01:20:38,230
We wouldn't be in this situation
if we had stayed still.

2012
01:20:38,300 --> 01:20:39,470
He's right too.

2013
01:20:39,470 --> 01:20:42,170
- If we didn't do anything...
- They wouldn't have taken action.

2014
01:20:42,170 --> 01:20:43,340
Exactly.

2015
01:20:43,340 --> 01:20:45,810
So they're copying us
now that we made the move.

2016
01:20:46,180 --> 01:20:48,480
I'd like to make a suggestion...

2017
01:20:48,480 --> 01:20:50,450
since the dynamics have changed.

2018
01:20:50,450 --> 01:20:52,380
They have five people now.

2019
01:20:52,780 --> 01:20:54,920
That means they have at least five lives.

2020
01:20:55,120 --> 01:20:58,350
We should go in before
the trade is over and start a war.

2021
01:20:58,350 --> 01:21:00,390
(Start a war.)

2022
01:21:08,260 --> 01:21:09,700
- What if they...
- Wait.

2023
01:21:09,700 --> 01:21:10,870
only relocated without the lives?

2024
01:21:10,870 --> 01:21:12,900
It's better for us
if they didn't take lives with them.

2025
01:21:12,900 --> 01:21:14,870
If we slash them in half
before they bring their lives,

2026
01:21:14,870 --> 01:21:16,340
one of them has to go home today.

2027
01:21:16,340 --> 01:21:17,610
- That's good. Let's do that.
- Yes.

2028
01:21:20,880 --> 01:21:23,680
(Trading session)

2029
01:21:24,450 --> 01:21:27,120
This is Leia, Team White's leader.

2030
01:21:28,380 --> 01:21:32,660
We wanted to
live peacefully with Team Gold,

2031
01:21:32,860 --> 01:21:35,630
the new members of our community.

2032
01:21:35,630 --> 01:21:38,030
We wanted to cooperate
and live a life without war.

2033
01:21:38,030 --> 01:21:41,100
But that didn't go as we planned.

2034
01:21:41,870 --> 01:21:45,340
We wanted to avoid war at all costs,
regardless of the reason.

2035
01:21:47,370 --> 01:21:49,140
I know this is all an excuse.

2036
01:21:54,310 --> 01:21:55,650
But I wanted to...

2037
01:21:56,580 --> 01:21:58,350
save everyone in Team White.

2038
01:22:01,750 --> 01:22:05,490
Team White declares war on Team Gold.

2039
01:22:08,390 --> 01:22:11,730
Today's war cost is 200 diamonds.

2040
01:22:12,560 --> 01:22:14,700
Write the amount on the voucher...

2041
01:22:14,700 --> 01:22:17,030
and submit it through the central box.

2042
01:22:19,740 --> 01:22:22,970
I paid the war cost of 200 diamonds.

2043
01:22:27,810 --> 01:22:30,050
The war cost has been paid.

2044
01:22:30,050 --> 01:22:31,780
(Team White has declared war
on Team Gold.)

2045
01:22:37,690 --> 01:22:41,620
Team White has declared war on Team Gold.

2046
01:22:41,660 --> 01:22:45,660
Community Town now enters a state of war.

2047
01:22:50,870 --> 01:22:52,840
- Well...
- Someone started a war.

2048
01:22:57,470 --> 01:23:01,340
Team White has declared war on Team Gold.

2049
01:23:01,980 --> 01:23:03,680
White declared it on us.

2050
01:23:03,980 --> 01:23:05,380
They put all their resources to Red...

2051
01:23:05,380 --> 01:23:07,020
or gave them to Black
for White to do this.

2052
01:23:07,020 --> 01:23:08,650
I know. We had to declare war first.

2053
01:23:08,650 --> 01:23:10,720
We could've eliminated them,
and now we're late again.

2054
01:23:10,720 --> 01:23:12,020
Compared to them,

2055
01:23:12,020 --> 01:23:14,720
our decision-making process is
too long and slow.

2056
01:23:14,820 --> 01:23:16,460
That's why they always get to us.

2057
01:23:17,090 --> 01:23:18,260
I was frustrated.

2058
01:23:18,660 --> 01:23:22,000
We had to make contact
and talk to other teams...

2059
01:23:22,000 --> 01:23:23,930
to persuade them.

2060
01:23:23,930 --> 01:23:27,170
But we always take so long
talking and planning among ourselves.

2061
01:23:27,170 --> 01:23:30,040
We lose time and miss opportunities.
It's a shame.

2062
01:23:30,410 --> 01:23:32,080
Up until now,

2063
01:23:32,080 --> 01:23:35,910
they pretended not to be seen as a team.

2064
01:23:35,910 --> 01:23:39,950
But now they're making it clear
they've allied together.

2065
01:23:40,020 --> 01:23:41,680
So there was a change.

2066
01:23:41,680 --> 01:23:45,860
I still don't know why they had to
declare war against us.

2067
01:23:45,990 --> 01:23:48,090
Did they not have enough lives
to make it past today?

2068
01:23:48,220 --> 01:23:51,560
But my calculations say otherwise.
If they're joining as one team,

2069
01:23:51,630 --> 01:23:54,760
three teams don't need lives.

2070
01:23:54,760 --> 01:23:58,700
I wouldn't be upset if they had
a valid reason for this war.

2071
01:23:58,700 --> 01:24:01,970
But as of now,
I can't see any reason for this.

2072
01:24:02,270 --> 01:24:03,970
I'm just so confused.

2073
01:24:04,110 --> 01:24:05,440
We are in a state of war.

2074
01:24:05,910 --> 01:24:08,410
All residents,
please go to your dormitory...

2075
01:24:08,410 --> 01:24:10,210
- and wait for further instructions.
- This is insane.

2076
01:24:10,980 --> 01:24:12,920
Yesterday, my identity was revealed,

2077
01:24:12,920 --> 01:24:15,820
as was Donkey's.

2078
01:24:15,890 --> 01:24:18,590
Then Maillard
and the weapon dealer join hands.

2079
01:24:18,760 --> 01:24:21,720
Leia, who lost a precious teammate
because of the weapon dealer,

2080
01:24:21,860 --> 01:24:24,330
joined hands
with the weapon dealer as well.

2081
01:24:24,330 --> 01:24:26,400
They've been at each other's throats,

2082
01:24:26,400 --> 01:24:30,130
but I guess they needed
some money in the end.

2083
01:24:30,130 --> 01:24:31,170
Come in.

2084
01:24:31,170 --> 01:24:32,240
(Dormitory for Red)

2085
01:24:32,770 --> 01:24:34,800
- Is this your first time here?
- It is.

2086
01:24:35,370 --> 01:24:36,640
I haven't had a chance.

2087
01:24:36,870 --> 01:24:38,240
So...

2088
01:24:38,670 --> 01:24:40,480
We won't have to produce...

2089
01:24:40,840 --> 01:24:42,150
credits or anything, right?

2090
01:24:42,310 --> 01:24:44,350
I'm not sure.
But we need to make a choice.

2091
01:24:44,350 --> 01:24:46,320
There will be
only one production site tomorrow anyway.

2092
01:24:46,320 --> 01:24:48,450
I'd like to win this war...

2093
01:24:48,480 --> 01:24:50,650
and see what resources they have.

2094
01:24:51,090 --> 01:24:53,120
Then I want to make a bid...

2095
01:24:53,120 --> 01:24:54,920
for an appropriate amount.

2096
01:24:54,920 --> 01:24:56,890
- We gave them so many resources.
- Right.

2097
01:24:57,290 --> 01:24:58,730
If they'd offered that...

2098
01:24:59,030 --> 01:25:02,230
when I went to the Center yesterday,
I would've taken it.

2099
01:25:02,370 --> 01:25:04,630
They might've won this...

2100
01:25:04,630 --> 01:25:06,340
- if they had made that decision...
- Right.

2101
01:25:06,870 --> 01:25:08,870
- and negotiated with us.
- Yes.

2102
01:25:08,870 --> 01:25:12,980
Right now, we have to fight in a war...

2103
01:25:13,210 --> 01:25:16,780
that we are not prepared for.

2104
01:25:16,910 --> 01:25:19,150
But I really want us to pull through.

2105
01:25:19,150 --> 01:25:20,220
At this point,

2106
01:25:20,220 --> 01:25:22,450
winning is our only option.

2107
01:25:22,450 --> 01:25:24,420
- Let's fight for our deaths.
- But would Leia win...

2108
01:25:24,420 --> 01:25:25,660
- if she went against us alone?
- No, wait.

2109
01:25:25,660 --> 01:25:27,360
- They teamed up.
- Her alliance is there.

2110
01:25:27,360 --> 01:25:29,230
- It's 6 to 5.
- Yes, it's 6 to 5.

2111
01:25:29,230 --> 01:25:32,430
We still have a shot at this.

2112
01:25:32,430 --> 01:25:35,360
We need to decide
if we're buying weapons now.

2113
01:25:35,630 --> 01:25:38,730
I don't think
it's a good idea to use weapons.

2114
01:25:38,730 --> 01:25:42,000
We'd just be giving
either Vector or Donkey the money.

2115
01:25:42,000 --> 01:25:46,140
It'll be better
not to play into their hands.

2116
01:25:46,380 --> 01:25:48,780
- Let's win this.
- Now that this is happening today,

2117
01:25:48,780 --> 01:25:51,910
- let's give it our all and do this.
- Yes.

2118
01:25:56,950 --> 01:25:59,560
Purchasing weapons
and forming alliances...

2119
01:25:59,560 --> 01:26:01,360
in a state of war is possible now.

2120
01:26:01,360 --> 01:26:02,360
Let's go.

2121
01:26:02,360 --> 01:26:04,030
Please visit the Center...

2122
01:26:04,030 --> 01:26:05,730
- if you would like to purchase weapons.
- Go.

2123
01:26:05,730 --> 01:26:07,830
- Let's go!
- Okay.

2124
01:26:08,060 --> 01:26:10,570
This is a lightning war. Darn it.

2125
01:26:12,070 --> 01:26:14,140
Let's just head there, just in case.

2126
01:26:14,140 --> 01:26:16,170
Yes, we'll see how they play things.

2127
01:26:16,170 --> 01:26:17,870
If you would like to form an alliance,

2128
01:26:17,870 --> 01:26:19,980
ring the bell in your dormitory...

2129
01:26:20,080 --> 01:26:23,010
to contact the other team.

2130
01:26:27,880 --> 01:26:30,090
I request an alliance with Team Red.

2131
01:26:34,260 --> 01:26:35,560
Quickly!

2132
01:26:37,790 --> 01:26:38,860
Gosh.

2133
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:41,660
- We have to accept the alliance.
- Where is everyone?

2134
01:26:41,660 --> 01:26:42,800
Why are you all so fast?

2135
01:26:50,540 --> 01:26:52,280
Oh, I can't see the weapon cost...

2136
01:26:52,510 --> 01:26:53,880
because I'm not in this war.

2137
01:26:54,780 --> 01:26:57,050
I'm not of use. They have to get here.

2138
01:26:59,450 --> 01:27:00,480
Leia!

2139
01:27:01,320 --> 01:27:02,520
- Yes?
- Come out.

2140
01:27:03,350 --> 01:27:04,790
I requested an alliance.

2141
01:27:05,390 --> 01:27:07,060
You have to accept first.

2142
01:27:07,060 --> 01:27:08,360
Don't weapons come first?

2143
01:27:08,360 --> 01:27:09,590
- Purchase weapons first?
- Yes.

2144
01:27:09,930 --> 01:27:11,530
Weapons? Did anyone come out?

2145
01:27:11,890 --> 01:27:13,030
No, they're not here.

2146
01:27:14,100 --> 01:27:15,160
Hurry.

2147
01:27:16,100 --> 01:27:17,370
What's taking her so long?

2148
01:27:19,740 --> 01:27:21,540
There's no rush, but still.

2149
01:27:24,040 --> 01:27:25,980
- Goodness.
- Gosh.

2150
01:27:26,640 --> 01:27:29,050
I guess you're experienced
in a state of war.

2151
01:27:29,450 --> 01:27:30,480
Shall we?

2152
01:27:31,650 --> 01:27:33,580
I'm glad everyone's energized now.

2153
01:27:33,580 --> 01:27:35,450
I like playing games like this.

2154
01:27:36,390 --> 01:27:37,920
I'm a warlord now.

2155
01:27:37,920 --> 01:27:39,290
(The diamond alliance arrives
at the Center first.)

2156
01:27:39,290 --> 01:27:40,360
Warlord Leia.

2157
01:27:40,360 --> 01:27:43,130
(State of War, Purchasing weapons,
Forming alliances)

2158
01:27:43,960 --> 01:27:46,530
Team White will purchase weapons.

2159
01:27:47,200 --> 01:27:48,970
Please check the weapon cost...

2160
01:27:48,970 --> 01:27:52,270
and tell us the class of weapons
you'd like to purchase.

2161
01:27:52,970 --> 01:27:54,370
It's 12 million, 8 million,

2162
01:27:54,370 --> 01:27:55,770
and five million. That's right.

2163
01:27:56,210 --> 01:28:00,340
I will purchase
all three classes of weapons.

2164
01:28:00,680 --> 01:28:04,350
You have selected
Class A, Class B, and Class C weapons.

2165
01:28:04,480 --> 01:28:07,250
Please submit the voucher
in the central box.

2166
01:28:14,360 --> 01:28:16,490
I'm sorry, but I need to make sure...

2167
01:28:17,790 --> 01:28:20,030
we win this war.
I'm purchasing all of them.

2168
01:28:20,030 --> 01:28:21,460
(25 million diamonds)

2169
01:28:21,460 --> 01:28:24,030
The weapon cost has been paid.

2170
01:28:24,170 --> 01:28:27,170
Please collect the weapons
from the central box.

2171
01:28:27,840 --> 01:28:30,340
Come on, we're all new to this,
and we're all older.

2172
01:28:30,340 --> 01:28:32,140
- Take it easy on us.
- We're not so young ourselves.

2173
01:28:32,140 --> 01:28:33,480
Sweetie, we gave birth too.

2174
01:28:33,480 --> 01:28:35,480
- I can't compete with that.
- Yes, we're parents.

2175
01:28:40,980 --> 01:28:42,390
Paul, come in.

2176
01:28:43,590 --> 01:28:45,760
Was the weapon cost set as we calculated?

2177
01:28:45,820 --> 01:28:47,390
Yes, about 25 million diamonds.

2178
01:28:47,390 --> 01:28:48,820
- Minus 200 diamonds.
- Right.

2179
01:28:50,460 --> 01:28:54,830
Team White and Team Red
will form an alliance.

2180
01:28:55,670 --> 01:28:59,370
Team White and Team Red
have formed an alliance.

2181
01:28:59,570 --> 01:29:00,970
- Now, the two teams...
- Let's do this.

2182
01:29:00,970 --> 01:29:02,410
- will fight the war together.
- Yes!

2183
01:29:02,410 --> 01:29:03,410
Great.

2184
01:29:04,140 --> 01:29:06,540
I think we'll win.

2185
01:29:06,810 --> 01:29:08,180
We have all three weapons.

2186
01:29:08,280 --> 01:29:10,680
And the headcount is
different from the first war.

2187
01:29:10,680 --> 01:29:12,720
We have one more member.

2188
01:29:13,080 --> 01:29:15,380
I know the initiator
shouldn't feel this way.

2189
01:29:15,380 --> 01:29:17,450
It's so hypocritical.

2190
01:29:18,050 --> 01:29:19,090
But I do feel sorry.

2191
01:29:19,890 --> 01:29:21,690
I wonder how high...

2192
01:29:21,690 --> 01:29:23,230
- the cost is.
- Right?

2193
01:29:23,290 --> 01:29:25,960
We would like to check the weapon cost.

2194
01:29:28,460 --> 01:29:31,130
- All weapons have been purchased.
- Eighty quintillion gold.

2195
01:29:31,130 --> 01:29:33,070
There are no weapons remaining.

2196
01:29:34,500 --> 01:29:35,600
Eighty quintillion?

2197
01:29:37,870 --> 01:29:40,280
- This is hilarious.
- It's so funny.

2198
01:29:40,340 --> 01:29:43,580
I think they tried...

2199
01:29:43,680 --> 01:29:45,110
to meet the amount.

2200
01:29:45,110 --> 01:29:47,920
- If it was distributed fairly,
- Yes.

2201
01:29:47,920 --> 01:29:49,420
- They must've met the amount.
- that's the amount...

2202
01:29:49,420 --> 01:29:51,090
going to the weapon dealer.

2203
01:29:51,090 --> 01:29:54,090
They're looking after Vector and Donkey.

2204
01:29:54,860 --> 01:29:56,860
Just wipe us out.

2205
01:29:56,860 --> 01:29:59,560
We're already getting wiped out.

2206
01:29:59,630 --> 01:30:01,300
If you're trying to wipe us out,

2207
01:30:01,330 --> 01:30:02,570
we'll play along.

2208
01:30:02,570 --> 01:30:04,030
Let's have some fun.

2209
01:30:07,500 --> 01:30:08,540
- It's chilly.
- Yes.

2210
01:30:08,540 --> 01:30:10,270
- It was hot last time we were here.
- I know.

2211
01:30:10,310 --> 01:30:11,870
- It's the rain.
- Right.

2212
01:30:12,110 --> 01:30:14,040
Who has weapons A, B, and C?

2213
01:30:14,040 --> 01:30:15,580
- Maillard.
- Maillard.

2214
01:30:15,680 --> 01:30:17,250
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

2215
01:30:17,250 --> 01:30:18,380
Let's go.

2216
01:30:19,880 --> 01:30:20,980
I can't believe we're back here.

2217
01:30:21,550 --> 01:30:26,460
(Battlefield)

2218
01:30:27,890 --> 01:30:29,560
What is this?

2219
01:30:40,670 --> 01:30:41,770
What's that?

2220
01:30:42,370 --> 01:30:43,510
What is this?

2221
01:30:43,510 --> 01:30:44,640
OX?

2222
01:30:44,740 --> 01:30:46,840
- It's the OX quiz.
- The OX quiz.

2223
01:30:46,840 --> 01:30:48,940
Isn't this a gavel?

2224
01:30:50,050 --> 01:30:53,020
- Wait, Luna. Was it done here?
- Yes.

2225
01:30:53,020 --> 01:30:54,580
- Is it the same place?
- Yes.

2226
01:31:01,790 --> 01:31:03,890
(Exclaiming)

2227
01:31:03,890 --> 01:31:05,530
It reminds me of "Gonjiam."

2228
01:31:07,300 --> 01:31:08,400
(Exclaiming)

2229
01:31:08,400 --> 01:31:09,800
It looks like an OX quiz.

2230
01:31:11,570 --> 01:31:13,770
It says Team Gold versus Team White.

2231
01:31:14,300 --> 01:31:15,970
Are we playing an OX quiz?

2232
01:31:16,410 --> 01:31:17,910
They look like they'd be good at it.

2233
01:31:18,410 --> 01:31:21,210
It was more organized than the first time.

2234
01:31:21,210 --> 01:31:22,710
I guess it's a quiz.

2235
01:31:22,750 --> 01:31:25,210
I thought it wouldn't be in my favor.

2236
01:31:25,210 --> 01:31:27,050
Because everyone in Team Gold is...

2237
01:31:27,080 --> 01:31:29,190
good at games.

2238
01:31:30,320 --> 01:31:32,760
That game is worth playing.

2239
01:31:32,890 --> 01:31:34,660
I'm the best at it.

2240
01:31:34,660 --> 01:31:36,760
There's no psychological pressure.

2241
01:31:37,430 --> 01:31:38,830
Today's battle is...

2242
01:31:38,830 --> 01:31:40,830
the Fact Land Grab.

2243
01:31:40,830 --> 01:31:42,100
- Fact.
- Fact Land Grab.

2244
01:31:42,100 --> 01:31:44,070
- Land Grab.
- Fact Land Grab.

2245
